# Compiled binaries, should anyone `go build` in place rather than `go run`.
#
# Go's module and build caches live in `~/go` and `~/.cache/go-build`, outside
# the checkout, so there is far less to exclude here than in a Cargo project —
# but a stray binary is still ours to keep out of somebody's first commit.
#
# This file ships WITH the seed and becomes the new repository's `.gitignore`.
/web
/worker

# AIR'S BUILD DIRECTORY. `air` compiles the service into `tmp/` on every save,
# so this is a binary rewritten several times a minute — committed once, it is a
# conflict on every future pull.
/tmp

# The database. `DATABASE_PATH` points at `db/app.sqlite3` and WAL makes it
# three files — somebody's local data, never a commit.
/db
